#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hail — one verb that delivers a pointer to any session the harness contract names: the inbox
socket on this Mac (any login: the login dirs share one registry), `codex queue` to a named thread,
`orca orchestration send`, else helm's Talk and file roads. No broker, no service. The Lookout and
Hail design, its section "Hail" and S2 (docs/crosstalk-2026-10-20.md on its branch).

    hail REF (--text T | --file F) [--kind event|report|ask] [--about REPO:BRANCH:DOC[#Dn]]
         [--thread ID] [--host here|<peer>] [--when now|idle] [--no-file] [--dry-run] [--json]
        REF as `harness status` takes it: a session id or a prefix of 6 or more, a session's title,
        a dispatch run's topic. --thread ID hails that Codex thread (REF is then only a label).
        Prints one record, {road, verdict, target, at, …}; verdict is delivered | queued | held |
        unreachable | refused (`dry-run` under --dry-run). Exit 0 delivered, queued, held or a dry
        run; 2 refused; 3 unreachable; 1 a usage error.
    hail subs [--fulfil] [--dry-run] [--json]
        The `--when idle` subscriptions, state_dir()/hail-subs.jsonl. --fulfil (the tick's) hails each
        row whose target is now idle, or has ended, and drops it; a row older than SUB_TTL_H is dropped
        unsent. Exit 0; 3 when a fulfilled row found no road.
    hail mail [--pull] [--dry-run] [--json]
        The mailbox, state_dir()/hail-mailbox.jsonl: the rows this Mac holds for sessions on other
        Macs. --pull (the bell's, `ask poll`, every host) fetches this Mac's own rows from each peer it
        has an ssh alias for, posts each by the socket road and settles it on the peer. A peer that does
        not answer is one line when it goes quiet and one when it answers again. Exit 0; 3 when a
        settle did not reach the peer (its rows settle from this Mac's ledger at their next take).
    hail mail --take HOST | --settle HOST --results JSON
        The sender's half of a pull, run on it over ssh: --take marks HOST's rows taken and prints
        them; --settle records what HOST did with each (a JSON list of {id, token, verdict, why};
        a pull sends it over stdin, ahead of this code).

The roads, in this order, the first whose preconditions hold:
    socket    a Claude Code session live on this Mac: the adapter's send() posts to its inbox, but only
              after re-reading its registry record and finding it idle for IDLE_S seconds or more —
              a post mid-turn lands at its next tool boundary. `delivered` is read back from the
              receiver (its transcript's enqueue, or its status turning busy), never from the
              socket, which answers nothing; nothing seen within HAIL_READBACK_S is `held`
    codex     --thread ID only: `codex queue` (the adapter lists a thread only while a turn is open). The
              thread's record is read first: one mid-turn is refused as a busy socket is (`--when idle`
              subscribes); the frame goes behind the adapter's peer mark, as Codex loads no K3 rule; and
              the vendor fence judges the thread's repo and the sender's (vendor-fence, 2026-10-29)
    orca      an Orca worker: its mailbox, or its terminal when idle
    talk      helm's asklib: spacesheep Talk to the target's page — any Mac, any harness, any login.
              The page is HAIL_SPACE, else this run's skipper page when the target is its skipper
              (DISPATCH_PLAN_SPACE), else the Mac's standing skipper's. A `--when idle` row keeps
              the HAIL_SPACE it was made under, so the tick's fulfil posts to that page, not to
              whatever its own environment names (skipper-resilience S6: wharf hails a scope's
              skipper on the page its record names). Sender unverified
    mailbox   --host PEER only, when no ssh reaches PEER from here (no alias, or ssh itself failed;
              never after PEER was reached, whose own roads ran there, nor after a timeout, which may
              come after its post) and PEER's pull was seen here within MAIL_SEEN_H (else
              `unreachable`, said: a typo, a cloud session or a Mac off for a day never pulls): a row
              in this Mac's mailbox addressed to the session on PEER, which PEER's bell pulls over its
              own alias to this Mac (`hail mail --pull`). Claude Code sessions only: the pull posts by
              the socket road there, under its idle and read-back rules, so a row waits at most one
              bell (5 minutes) and the next idle moment. The take is recorded here before PEER posts,
              so two pulls never take one row at once; a take not settled in HAIL_MAIL_TAKE_S (900 s) is taken
              again, and PEER's ledger of what it posted settles it then without a second post.
              A row whose session has ended on PEER (its transcript is there, no registry holds a
              live process for it) comes back `ended`: this Mac's hail.jsonl gets a line with road
              mailbox and verdict ended, which is how a sender learns its target exited without a
              renewal. A session PEER never ran is not ended, only unknown: the row waits, and
              expires unsent after SUB_TTL_H. Known limitation: a receiver with no ssh alias to the
              sender's host (a claude.ai/code cloud session) never pulls (the charterer design's S2)
    file      helm's asklib: a line its next prompt prints; this Mac, a live process; wakes nobody
              (--no-file skips it: for a target that never reads that queue, a scope's skipper)
A refused road stops the hail (a busy session is waited for, never routed around); a held or
unreachable one falls through to the next. Claude Code's SendMessage is never a road: it is a model's
tool, and only within one login.

Which roads, in which order: helm's surfaces.json, its `hail.roads` row (SURFACES_FILE, else the
config dir's helm/surfaces.json, the file helm's bin/surfaces.py reads and validates); a missing
file or row reads as ROADS. A road left out is never taken. The target's own road (socket, codex or
orca: one applies to a session) always goes first whatever its place, since its refusal of a busy
session must stop the hail; talk, mailbox and file follow in the row's order.

--host PEER: the adapter roads run on PEER over ssh (bin/harness's peers and alias; this code and the
adapters go over stdin, as `harness status --host` does), then Talk from here. ssh runs one way: a
peer this Mac has no alias for gets Talk, or the mailbox, which that peer pulls over its own alias.

The frame is fixed text; the caller's words are a pointer, not content:
    HAIL <kind> from <sender> — <text> — about <repo>:<branch>:<doc>#<Dn> @<sha>
--about names where to look, and hail reads only the branch's commit for @<sha>: an answer's words
never ride in a hail (K13). A text that carries an answer block or a relayed answer is refused, and
one over TEXT_MAX characters too. A hail is data to its receiver (K3): it may name a doc, a commit,
a run or a page; it approves nothing, and the receiver's own permissions decide what it does.

--when idle: hailed now when the target is idle; while it works, the hail is a row in
state_dir()/hail-subs.jsonl, which `hail subs --fulfil` sends once the target goes idle or ends.
Every hail, sent, refused or subscribed, is a line in state_dir()/hail.jsonl (cost: none — no model
call is made here). state_dir() is keel's: MEMO_STATE_DIR, else ~/.local/state/memo.

Tests stand in: HAIL_ASKLIB (asklib's path), HAIL_READBACK_S, HAIL_MAIL_TAKE_S, HAIL_MAIL_SEEN_S, HARNESS_SSH,
HARNESS_CODEX, HARNESS_ORCA, HARNESS_HOST, HARNESS_PEER_<HOST>, ASK_SESSIONS_DIR, SURFACES_FILE;
`hail mail --pull` reads ASK_POLL_DEADLINE, which `ask poll` gives each job.
Python 3.9, stdlib only.
"""
import fcntl
import glob
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import types
import uuid

if "__file__" in globals():   # here, not on a peer from stdin: the regatta core on the path, for asklib
    sys.path.insert(1, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))), "lib"))
    try:
        import core_path
        core_path.add()
    except ImportError:
        pass

USAGE = __doc__.split("\n\n")[1] if __doc__ else "hail REF --text T"
KINDS = ("event", "report", "ask")
ROAD = {"claude-code": "socket", "codex": "codex", "orca": "orca"}
IDLE_S = 60         # the quiet a socket post needs: the contract line's, fixed
TEXT_MAX = 400       # a pointer's length: a hail names where to look, it never carries the thing
SUB_TTL_H = 72       # a subscription whose target never went idle in three days is dropped unsent
# what an answer looks like in a D-list doc or a relay (asklib's RELAYED_HEAD_RE): never in a frame
# (anywhere on a line: the frame flattens whitespace, so a relay quoted mid-line counts too)
ANSWER_RE = re.compile(r"➤\s*Answer|Relayed from .*\): ", re.I)
FRAME_MAX = TEXT_MAX + 400   # the fixed prefix, the sender's name and an --about: a peer half refuses more
FRAME_RE = re.compile(r"^HAIL (event|report|ask) from .+ — ")
EXIT = {"delivered": 0, "queued": 0, "held": 0, "dry-run": 0, "refused": 2, "unreachable": 3}
# every road, in the order a missing surfaces.json row reads as (the charterer design's S2: mailbox
# after talk); helm's surfaces.KNOWN["hail.roads"] holds the same names
ROADS = ("socket", "codex", "orca", "talk", "mailbox", "file")
RELAY = ("talk", "mailbox", "file")   # the roads after the target's own, in the row's order
HOST_RE = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,62}$")
# a frame is one line: a newline (or any control or line-separator character) would carry a second
# line that does not read as a HAIL line (the S2 landing review: a forged mailbox row)
CTRL_RE = re.compile("[\x00-\x1f\x7f\x85\u2028\u2029]")
MAIL_SEEN_H = 24     # a host whose pull this Mac has not seen in a day gets no row: `unreachable`, said


def warn(msg):
    print("hail: %s" % msg, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)


def embedded():
    """{"harness": source, "adapters": {file: source}} when this copy runs on a peer from stdin."""
    return globals().get("HAIL_EMBEDDED")


def here_bin():
    return os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))


_H = []


def harness():
    """bin/harness as a module: its adapters, its pick() and its peers — one reading of REF and of
    the hosts for both verbs. On a peer, from the source that came over stdin."""
    if _H:
        return _H[0]
    emb = embedded()
    if emb is not None:
        mod = types.ModuleType("harness_mod")
        mod.HARNESS_EMBEDDED = emb["adapters"]
        exec(compile(emb["harness"], "harness", "exec"), mod.__dict__)
    else:
        path = os.path.join(here_bin(), "harness")
        loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("harness_mod", path)
        mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader("harness_mod", loader))
        loader.exec_module(mod)
    _H.append(mod)
    return mod


_ASK = []


def asklib():
    """helm's asklib (the Talk and file roads), or None — named once, never a trace. HAIL_ASKLIB,
    else the core's tool() lookup."""
    if _ASK:
        return _ASK[0]
    mod, path = None, os.environ.get("HAIL_ASKLIB")
    if not path:
        try:
            import common
            p = common.tool("asklib.py")
            path = str(p) if p else None
        except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001 — no core: the roads it carries are skipped, said
            path = None
    if path and os.path.isfile(path):
        try:
            loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("asklib", path)
            mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader("asklib", loader))
            loader.exec_module(mod)
        except Exception as e:   # noqa: BLE001
            warn("asklib at %s did not load (%s): the talk and file roads are skipped" % (path, e))
            mod = None
    _ASK.append(mod)
    return mod


def state_dir():
    """keel's per-Mac state dir (MEMO_STATE_DIR moves it), where the lookout keeps its memory too."""
    return os.environ.get("MEMO_STATE_DIR") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".local", "state", "memo")


def env_float(name, default):
    """A number of seconds from NAME, else DEFAULT (a value that is no number reads as the default)."""
    try:
        return float(os.environ.get(name) or default)
    except ValueError:
        return float(default)


def mail_take_s():
    """How long a take stands unsettled before another pull may take the row: a pull posts each row
    with a read-back of HAIL_READBACK_S, so a quarter hour is far past any live one."""
    return env_float("HAIL_MAIL_TAKE_S", 900)


def surfaces_file():
    """helm's surfaces.json, as its bin/surfaces.py names it: SURFACES_FILE, else the config dir's."""
    if os.environ.get("SURFACES_FILE"):
        return os.environ["SURFACES_FILE"]
    cfg = os.environ.get("REGATTA_CONFIG") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".config", "regatta")
    return os.path.join(os.path.expanduser(cfg), "helm", "surfaces.json")


ROADS_UNREAD = []   # set by roads(): the row was there and did not read (no road until it does)
SID_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_-]{5,}$")   # a session id: no glob character reaches a path pattern


def roads():
    """The roads this hail may take, in order: surfaces.json's hail.roads, else ROADS (no file, no
    `hail` seam, no `roads` row). The row only narrows, so a shape that does not read narrows to no
    road, said, never to every road (AGENTS.md's trap); a bare name reads as a list of one (surfaces.py's
    validate refuses it on a write). A name hail does not know is named and skipped."""
    try:
        with open(surfaces_file()) as f:
            data = json.load(f)
    except OSError as e:
        if isinstance(e, FileNotFoundError) and not os.path.lexists(surfaces_file()):
            return list(ROADS)   # no file at all: the only shape that widens
        warn("%s cannot be read (%s): no hail road is taken" % (surfaces_file(), e.strerror or e))
        ROADS_UNREAD.append(True)
        return []
    except ValueError:
        warn("%s does not parse: no hail road is taken" % surfaces_file())
        ROADS_UNREAD.append(True)
        return []
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        warn("%s is no object: no hail road is taken" % surfaces_file())
        ROADS_UNREAD.append(True)
        return []
    if "hail" not in data:
        return list(ROADS)
    seam = data["hail"]
    if not isinstance(seam, dict):
        warn("%s: hail is no object: no hail road is taken" % surfaces_file())
        ROADS_UNREAD.append(True)
        return []
    if "roads" not in seam:
        return list(ROADS)
    row = seam["roads"]
    if isinstance(row, str):
        row = [row]
    if not isinstance(row, list) or not all(isinstance(x, str) for x in row):
        warn("%s: hail.roads is no list of road names: no hail road is taken" % surfaces_file())
        ROADS_UNREAD.append(True)
        return []
    bad = [x for x in row if x not in ROADS]
    if bad:
        warn("%s: hail.roads names %s, which hail does not know: skipped" % (surfaces_file(), ", ".join(bad)))
    return [x for x in row if x in ROADS]


def log(rec):
    try:
        os.makedirs(state_dir(), exist_ok=True)
        with open(os.path.join(state_dir(), "hail.jsonl"), "a") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
    except OSError as e:
        warn("could not log the hail: %s" % e)


# ---- the frame -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

def sessions_dir():
    return os.environ.get("ASK_SESSIONS_DIR") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".claude", "sessions")


def sender():
    """Who hails: HAIL_FROM, else this session's title or id, else a script on this Mac."""
    if os.environ.get("HAIL_FROM"):
        return os.environ["HAIL_FROM"]
    sid = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID")
    if sid:
        for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(sessions_dir(), "*.json")):
            try:
                with open(p) as f:
                    d = json.load(f)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                continue
            if isinstance(d, dict) and d.get("sessionId") == sid and d.get("name"):
                return "%s (%s)" % (d["name"], sid[:8])
        return "session %s" % sid[:8]
    return "a script on %s" % harness().machine()


def parse_about(about):
    """REPO:BRANCH:DOC[#Dn] → dict, or exits. A branch holds slashes, never a colon."""
    # DOC is a path, no spaces: the frame carries --about as given, so free text there would get
    # past K13 and TEXT_MAX (B review, 2026-10-22)
    m = re.match(r"^([^:\s]+):([^:\s]+):([^#\s]+)(?:#(D\d+))?$", about or "")
    if not m or len(about) > 300 or ANSWER_RE.search(about):
        sys.exit("hail: --about is REPO:BRANCH:DOC[#Dn] (got %r)" % about)
    return {"repo": m.group(1), "branch": m.group(2), "doc": m.group(3), "item": m.group(4)}


def repo_dir(repo):
    """A repo named by absolute or ~ path, or by its name in the core's registry (cloned as
    PROJECTS/<name>, common.cloned_repos()'s rule), or None. Never against the caller's cwd."""
    if repo.startswith(("/", "~")):
        p = os.path.expanduser(repo)
        return p if os.path.isdir(p) else None
    try:
        import common
        return next((str(p) for p in common.cloned_repos() if p.name == repo), None)
    except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001 — no core or no registry: no @sha, said in the record
        return None


def sender_fenced(paths):
    """True when any of PATHS (the sender's side of a hail) is confidential or guarded, or that cannot be
    told (no core, a torn or unwalkable registry, an unknown path): a peer's non-Claude road then refuses
    (the vendor fence's cross-host half; the peer cannot judge a path on this Mac)."""
    try:
        import common
        reg, torn = common.read_registry()
        return bool(torn) or any(not p or common.fenced_scopes(p, reg or {}) for p in paths)
    except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001 — never known open
        return True


def sha_of(about):
    """The branch's commit, short: origin's when the repo has it, else the local branch's; or None.
    Only the commit is read, never the doc: its answers stay in the repo."""
    d = repo_dir(about["repo"])
    if not d:
        return None
    for ref in ("refs/remotes/origin/" + about["branch"], "refs/heads/" + about["branch"]):
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", d, "rev-parse", "--short", "--verify", "-q", ref],
                               capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
            return None
        if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip():
            return r.stdout.strip()
    return None


def frame(kind, text, about, who):
    out = "HAIL %s from %s — %s" % (kind, who, " ".join(text.split()))
    if about:
        out += " — about %s:%s:%s%s" % (about["repo"], about["branch"], about["doc"], "#" + about["item"] if about["item"] else "")
        if about.get("sha"):
            out += " @" + about["sha"]
    return out


def text_refusal(text):
    if not text.strip():
        return "the text is empty"
    if len(text) > TEXT_MAX:
        return "the text is %d characters, over %d: a hail is a pointer — name the doc, commit or page instead" % (len(text), TEXT_MAX)
    if ANSWER_RE.search(text):
        return "the text carries an answer: an answer's words never ride in a hail (K13) — point at the doc with --about"
    return None


# ---- the roads -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

def target_of(args):
    """(record, None) or (None, why): what REF names on this Mac, through bin/harness's pick()."""
    H = harness()
    if args.get("thread"):
        # the thread's own record (the codex adapter's V3: a harness run's, else Codex's store), so the busy
        # check runs as for any session; one Codex never listed is `unknown`, which codex queue then answers
        ctx = H.Ctx()
        mod = ctx.adapter("codex")
        found = [c for c in (mod.candidates(ctx, args["thread"]) if mod else []) if c.get("session_id") == args["thread"]]
        # every `harness resume` writes a record under the thread's id, oldest first: a turn still open in any
        # of them makes the thread busy, else the newest is what the thread is now
        open_ = [c for c in found if c.get("state") in ("working", "submitted")]
        pick = (open_ or found)[-1] if found else None
        rec = dict(pick) if pick else {"harness": "codex", "session_id": args["thread"], "state": "unknown"}
        if found and rec.get("state") not in ("working", "submitted"):
            # a thread between turns reads `completed` (or failed, canceled) in Codex's store, and is what
            # `codex queue` wakes: only a turn still open makes it busy, never "ended"
            rec["state"] = "idle"
        rec.setdefault("title", args.get("ref"))
        return rec, None
    ctx = H.Ctx()
    cands = H.local_candidates(H.adapters(), ctx, args["ref"])
    rec, many = H.pick(cands, args["ref"])
    if rec is None and many:
        return None, "%d live sessions answer to %r — name one by session id" % (len(many), args["ref"])
    if rec is None:
        return None, None
    return rec, None


def adapter_road(rec, msg):
    """(road, result) of the record's own harness, or (None, None) when it has no send()."""
    H = harness()
    ctx = H.Ctx()
    mod = ctx.adapter(rec.get("harness"))
    if mod is None or not hasattr(mod, "send"):
        return None, None
    try:
        return ROAD.get(rec.get("harness"), rec.get("harness")), mod.send(ctx, rec, msg)
    except Exception as e:   # noqa: BLE001 — an adapter's failure is that road's, the next is tried
        # raised: whether a post went out before it is not known (the mailbox keeps its provisional mark)
        return ROAD.get(rec.get("harness"), rec.get("harness")), {"verdict": "unreachable", "why": "%s" % e, "raised": True}


def talk_space(sid, space=None):
    """The Talk page a hail to SID posts on: SPACE (a subscription's, recorded from the HAIL_SPACE it
    was made under), else HAIL_SPACE, else the skipper pages below; None when none names one."""
    if space:
        return space
    if os.environ.get("HAIL_SPACE"):
        return os.environ["HAIL_SPACE"]
    if sid and sid in (os.environ.get("DISPATCH_SKIPPER"), os.environ.get("DISPATCH_MANAGER")):
        return os.environ.get("DISPATCH_PLAN_SPACE")
    ask = asklib()
    sm = ask.standing_skipper() if ask and hasattr(ask, "standing_skipper") else None
    if sm and sm.get("manager") == sid:
        return sm.get("space")
    return None


def relay_roads(sid, msg, tried, roads=("talk", "file")):
    """The asklib roads, Talk then file: (road, result) of the first that takes it, or (None, None)."""
    ask = asklib()
    if ask is None:
        tried.extend([name, "helm's asklib is not installed"] for name in roads)
        return None, None
    if not sid:
        tried.extend([name, "no session id to address"] for name in roads)
        return None, None
    ctx = {"manager": sid, "space": talk_space(sid, msg.get("space")), "session": os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID")}
    for name in roads:
        b = ask.BACKENDS.get(name)
        if b is None:
            tried.append([name, "asklib has no %s backend" % name])
            continue
        ok, why = b.available(ctx)
        if not ok:
            tried.append([name, why])
            continue
        if msg.get("dry"):
            return name, {"verdict": "dry-run", "why": why}
        verdict, detail = b.send(ctx, msg["frame"])
        if verdict == "unreachable":
            tried.append([name, detail])
            continue
        # Talk's `sent` is the page's thread taking it; the session reads it when it listens
        return name, {"verdict": "queued", "why": detail}
    return None, None


def bundle():
    """This file with harness's and the adapters' sources in front: what a peer's `python3 -` runs."""
    H = harness()
    with open(os.path.join(here_bin(), "harness")) as f:
        hsrc = f.read()
    with open(os.path.abspath(__file__)) as f:
        me = f.read()
    # ascii(): one line of the whole harness, non-ASCII escaped — Python 3.9 reading source from stdin
    # failed "Non-UTF-8 code" on the literal form (test_hail.sh, 2026-10-21)
    return "HAIL_EMBEDDED = %s\n%s" % (ascii({"harness": hsrc, "adapters": H.adapter_sources()}), me)


PEER_MARK = "hail: the peer half runs"   # its first stderr line: proof the code ran there, whatever ssh exits


def on_peer(host, alias, argv, src=None, want=dict, quiet=False, timeout=90):
    """This code runs on HOST with ARGV: (its JSON answer, None, True) or (None, why, connected).
    SRC is what goes over stdin (bundle(), the adapter roads'; mail_bundle(), the mailbox's halves);
    WANT the answer's type; TIMEOUT the call's whole time; QUIET keeps a failed call's stderr off this run's (the pull's take, every
    bell: its last line goes into WHY, which the pull says once). CONNECTED is False only when ssh itself failed (it could not start, or
    exited 255 with nothing on stdout and no PEER_MARK on stderr): a timeout or a garbled answer may come after the code ran
    there, so the mailbox never writes a second copy of what the peer may have posted."""
    cmd = "python3 - " + " ".join(shlex.quote(a) for a in argv)
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([harness().SSH, "-o", "BatchMode=yes", "-o", "ConnectTimeout=6", alias, cmd],
                           input=bundle() if src is None else src, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)
    except OSError as e:
        return None, "%s did not answer: %s" % (host, e), False
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:
        return None, "%s did not answer in time: %s" % (host, e), True
    errs = [l for l in (r.stderr or "").splitlines() if l.strip()]
    ran = PEER_MARK in errs
    errs = [l for l in errs if l != PEER_MARK]
    try:
        d = json.loads(r.stdout)
        ok = isinstance(d, want)
    except ValueError:
        d, ok = None, False
    if ok or not quiet:
        for line in errs:
            print("%s: %s" % (host, line), file=sys.stderr)
    if ok:
        return d, None, True
    tail = (": " + errs[-1].strip()[:160]) if quiet and errs else ""
    if d is not None:
        return None, "%s answered no record%s" % (host, tail), True
    return None, "%s did not answer (ssh %s, exit %s)%s" % (host, alias, r.returncode, tail), bool(ran or r.returncode != 255 or r.stdout.strip())


def deliver(args, msg):
    """One hail, now: the record (without `at`), every road tried in order."""
    H = harness()
    me = H.machine()
    host = args.get("host") or "here"
    rec_out = {"road": None, "verdict": "unreachable", "target": args.get("thread") or args["ref"],
               "host": me if host in ("here", me) else host, "kind": msg["kind"], "frame": msg["frame"], "why": None, "tried": []}
    tried = rec_out["tried"]
    sid, held, answered = args.get("thread") or args["ref"], None, False
    allowed = list(ROADS) if msg.get("roads") is None else msg["roads"]   # [] is a row that allows no road

    if host not in ("here", me):
        alias = H.peers().get(host)
        if alias is None:
            tried.append(["ssh", "no ssh alias from %s to %s: ssh runs one way; Talk or the mailbox only" % (me, host)])
        else:
            argv = ["--peer-half", args["ref"], "--text", args["text"], "--kind", msg["kind"], "--frame", msg["frame"],
                    "--roads", ",".join(allowed)]
            argv += (["--thread", args["thread"]] if args.get("thread") else []) + (["--dry-run"] if msg.get("dry") else [])
            # the sender's paths mean nothing on the peer: judged here, and only the verdict goes over
            argv += ["--sender-fenced"] if sender_fenced(msg.get("fence_paths") or [msg.get("sender_cwd") or os.getcwd()]) else []
            got, why, connected = on_peer(host, alias, argv)
            if why:
                tried.append(["ssh", why])
                answered = connected   # the peer half may have run: no mailbox copy beside its post
            else:
                answered = True   # the peer's own roads were tried there: no mailbox row for what it judged
                tried.extend(got.get("tried") or [])
                sid = got.get("target") or sid
                rec_out["target"] = sid
                if got.get("verdict") in ("delivered", "queued", "refused", "dry-run"):
                    got.update(host=host, tried=tried, frame=msg["frame"], kind=msg["kind"])
                    return got
                if got.get("verdict") == "held":
                    held = got
    else:
        rec, why = target_of(args)
        if why:
            rec_out.update(verdict="refused", why=why)
            return rec_out
        if rec is not None:
            sid = rec.get("session_id") or sid
            rec_out["target"] = sid
            rec_out["target_name"] = rec.get("title")
            if sid and sid == os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID"):
                rec_out.update(verdict="refused", why="a session does not hail itself")
                return rec_out
            own = ROAD.get(rec.get("harness"), rec.get("harness"))
            if rec.get("state") in H.FINAL:
                tried.append(["adapter", "%s has ended (%s)" % (sid, rec.get("state"))])
            elif own in ROADS and own not in allowed:
                tried.append([own, "not in surfaces.json's hail.roads"])
            else:
                road, res = adapter_road(rec, msg)
                if road is None:
                    tried.append([rec.get("harness") or "adapter", "this harness has no send()"])
                elif res["verdict"] in ("delivered", "queued", "refused", "dry-run"):
                    rec_out.update(road=road, verdict=res["verdict"], why=res["why"])
                    if res.get("busy"):
                        rec_out["busy"] = True   # a refusal that waits (a Codex thread mid-turn): --when idle subscribes
                    return rec_out
                else:
                    tried.append([road, res["why"]])
                    if res["verdict"] == "held":
                        held = dict(rec_out, road=road, verdict="held", why=res["why"])
        else:
            tried.append(["adapter", "no session here answers to %r" % args["ref"]])
    if args.get("peer-half"):
        return held or rec_out

    # after a held post Talk only, as the design's Risks line says: the file road reaches every live
    # session at its next prompt, beside the socket copy the owner may still release
    # --no-file: a target that never reads the file queue (a scope's skipper, S6) — a line there would
    # read as delivered and wait for a prompt that never comes
    relay = [r for r in allowed if r in RELAY]
    if held:
        relay = [r for r in relay if r == "talk"]   # a held post may still be released: no second copy
    if msg.get("no_file"):
        relay = [r for r in relay if r != "file"]
    for name in relay:
        if name != "mailbox":
            road, res = relay_roads(sid, msg, tried, (name,))
        elif host in ("here", me):
            continue   # a session on this Mac: its socket road was the mailbox's own, tried above
        else:
            road, res = mailbox_road(host, sid, args, dict(msg, roads=allowed), answered, tried)
        if road:
            rec_out.update(road=road, verdict=res["verdict"], why=res["why"])
            return rec_out
    if held:
        held["tried"] = tried
        return held
    rec_out["why"] = "every road refused it"
    return rec_out


# ---- subscriptions -------------------------------------------------------------------------

def subs_path():
    return os.path.join(state_dir(), "hail-subs.jsonl")


class SubsLock:
    """One writer of a rows file at a time (hail-subs.jsonl by default: the tick's fulfil and a
    session's subscribe; the mailbox's: a hail's post, a peer's take and settle)."""
    def __init__(self, path=None):
        self.path = path

    def __enter__(self):
        os.makedirs(state_dir(), exist_ok=True)
        self.fd = os.open((self.path or subs_path()) + ".lock", os.O_CREAT | os.O_RDWR, 0o600)
        fcntl.flock(self.fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *exc):
        fcntl.flock(self.fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
        os.close(self.fd)


def read_subs(path=None):
    """The rows; a line that does not parse is skipped with a warning, never the whole file, or the
    next write would drop every row."""
    rows, path = [], path or subs_path()
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            for n, l in enumerate(f, 1):
                if not l.strip().startswith("{"):
                    continue
                try:
                    rows.append(json.loads(l))
                except ValueError:
                    warn("%s line %d does not parse: skipped" % (path, n))
    except OSError:
        pass
    return rows


def write_subs(rows, path=None):
    path = path or subs_path()
    tmp = "%s.%d.tmp" % (path, os.getpid())
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        for r in rows:
            f.write(json.dumps(r, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def subscribe(args, msg, rec):
    row = {"id": uuid.uuid4().hex[:12], "at": int(time.time()), "ref": args["ref"], "target": rec.get("target"),
           "thread": args.get("thread"), "host": args.get("host") or "here", "kind": msg["kind"],
           "text": args["text"], "frame": msg["frame"], "waiting_on": rec.get("why"), "sender_cwd": msg.get("sender_cwd"),
           "fence_paths": msg.get("fence_paths")}
    if msg.get("space"):
        row["space"] = msg["space"]   # the page the fulfil posts to: this caller's, not the tick's
    if msg.get("no_file"):
        row["no_file"] = True
    if not msg.get("dry"):
        with SubsLock():
            write_subs(read_subs() + [row])
    return dict(rec, road="subs", verdict="dry-run" if msg.get("dry") else "queued", sub=row["id"],
                why="subscribed until %s goes idle (%s)" % (rec.get("target"), rec.get("why")))


def cmd_subs(args):
    rows = read_subs()
    if not args.get("fulfil"):
        if args.get("json"):
            print(json.dumps(rows, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))
        elif not rows:
            print("no hail subscriptions")
        else:
            for r in rows:
                print("%s  %s  %-10s %s  %s" % (r.get("id"), time.strftime("%m-%d %H:%M", time.localtime(r.get("at") or 0)),
                                               r.get("host"), r.get("target") or r.get("ref"), r.get("kind")))
        return 0
    dry = bool(args.get("dry-run"))
    out, rc, done, allowed = [], 0, set(), roads()
    if ROADS_UNREAD and not allowed:   # no road until the file reads: every row waits, none is dropped
        print("hail subs: %s does not read: the subscriptions wait for the next pass" % surfaces_file())
        return 0
    # the rows are read under the lock and delivered outside it: a socket readback or an ssh road can
    # take a minute, and a session's subscribe() would wait on the lock that long
    with SubsLock():
        rows = read_subs()
    for r in rows:
        try:
            if time.time() - (r.get("at") or 0) > SUB_TTL_H * 3600:
                res = {"road": None, "verdict": "unreachable", "target": r.get("target"), "why": "expired after %d h unsent" % SUB_TTL_H,
                       "sub": r.get("id"), "tried": []}
            else:
                a = {"ref": r.get("target") or r.get("ref"), "thread": r.get("thread"), "host": r.get("host"), "text": r.get("text")}
                msg = {"kind": r.get("kind") or "event", "frame": r.get("frame"), "dry": dry, "idle_s": IDLE_S, "roads": allowed,
                       "space": r.get("space"), "no_file": bool(r.get("no_file")), "sender_cwd": r.get("sender_cwd"),
                       # a row from before the fence names no paths: judged as unknown (refused), never the tick's cwd
                       "fence_paths": r.get("fence_paths") or [r.get("sender_cwd")]}
                res = deliver(a, msg)
                res["sub"] = r.get("id")
        except Exception as e:   # noqa: BLE001 — one bad row never costs the pass: it stays for the next
            res = {"road": None, "verdict": "refused", "target": r.get("target"), "why": "fulfil failed: %s" % e,
                   "sub": r.get("id"), "tried": [], "kept": True}
        busy = res["verdict"] == "refused" and not res.get("kept") and (res.get("road") in ("socket", "orca") or res.get("busy"))
        if busy or res.get("kept"):
            res["kept"] = True   # still working: the next pass tries again
        else:
            done.add(r.get("id"))
        res["at"] = int(time.time())
        if not dry and not busy:   # a target still at work is no news: one line a tick for 72 h would bury the log
            log(res)
        if res["verdict"] == "unreachable":
            rc = 3
        out.append(res)
    if not dry and done:
        with SubsLock():   # the rows as they are now, less the ones handled: a subscribe meanwhile stays
            write_subs([r for r in read_subs() if r.get("id") not in done])
    if args.get("json"):
        print(json.dumps(out, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))
    else:
        for res in out:
            print("%s  %s %s via %s%s" % (res.get("sub"), res.get("target"), res["verdict"], res.get("road") or "-",
                                          " (kept)" if res.get("kept") else ""))
    return rc


# ---- the mailbox (the charterer design's S2) -----------------------------------------------
#
# The sender's side: mailbox_road() writes a row, `hail mail --take` and `--settle` run here over a
# peer's ssh. The receiver's side: `hail mail --pull`, from its bell, posts each row it took by the
# socket road. A row: {id, at, host (the receiver), target, kind, frame, from, state waiting|taken,
# token and taken_at while taken, last: why the latest pull kept it, roads: the sender's hail.roads,
# which the receiver honours as the peer half honours --roads}.
# Beside it, on the sender: hail-mailbox-pulls.json, {host: when its pull last took here} (a row is
# written only for a host seen pulling). On the receiver: hail-mailbox-done.json, {"<sender>:<id>":
# the final verdict}, marked `held` right before the post and replaced by the verdict after it, so a
# row whose settle was lost, or whose pull was killed mid-post, is settled from it on its next take and
# never posted twice (at most once: a pull killed between the mark and the post loses that row); and hail-mailbox-peers.json, each
# peer's last answer, so an asleep peer is one line when it goes quiet, not one every bell.

FINAL_MAIL = ("delivered", "held", "ended", "unreachable", "refused")   # a settled row leaves the box


def mail_path(name="hail-mailbox.jsonl"):
    return os.path.join(state_dir(), name)


def read_json(path, default):
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            d = json.load(f)
        return d if isinstance(d, type(default)) else default
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return default


def write_json(path, data):
    os.makedirs(state_dir(), exist_ok=True)
    tmp = "%s.%d.tmp" % (path, os.getpid())
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(data, f, ensure_ascii=False)
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def mail_seen_s():
    return env_float("HAIL_MAIL_SEEN_S", MAIL_SEEN_H * 3600)


def mailbox_road(host, sid, args, msg, answered, tried):
    """(road, result) when the row is written, or (None, None) with the reason in TRIED. A row is
    written only for a host whose pull this Mac has seen within mail_seen_s(): one that never pulls
    (a typo, a cloud session, a Mac asleep for a day) is `unreachable`, so a caller still falls back
    (keel's lookout card, the stall road), never a `queued` that nothing will fetch."""
    if answered:
        tried.append(["mailbox", "%s was reached over ssh: its own roads ran there" % host])
        return None, None
    if args.get("thread"):
        tried.append(["mailbox", "a Codex thread: the mailbox posts to Claude Code sessions only"])
        return None, None
    if "socket" not in (msg.get("roads") or []):
        tried.append(["mailbox", "the receiver posts a row by the socket road, which hail.roads leaves out here"])
        return None, None
    peer = (host or "").lower()
    if not HOST_RE.match(peer):
        tried.append(["mailbox", "%r is no host name" % host])
        return None, None
    me = harness().machine()
    seen = read_json(mail_path("hail-mailbox-pulls.json"), {}).get(peer)
    if not isinstance(seen, (int, float)) or time.time() - seen > mail_seen_s():
        tried.append(["mailbox", "no pull from %s seen on %s in %d h: it has no ssh alias here, or is off" % (peer, me, mail_seen_s() // 3600)])
        return None, None
    why = "in %s's mailbox for %s: its bell pulls it within 5 minutes and posts it once the session is idle" % (me, peer)
    if msg.get("dry"):
        return "mailbox", {"verdict": "dry-run", "why": why}
    row = {"id": uuid.uuid4().hex[:12], "at": int(time.time()), "host": peer, "target": sid, "kind": msg["kind"],
           "frame": msg["frame"], "from": me, "state": "waiting", "roads": list(msg.get("roads") or [])}
    try:
        with SubsLock(mail_path()):
            write_subs(expire(read_subs(mail_path()), time.time()) + [row], mail_path())
    except OSError as e:
        tried.append(["mailbox", "the mailbox could not be written: %s" % e])
        return None, None
    return "mailbox", {"verdict": "queued", "why": why + " (row %s)" % row["id"]}


def expire(rows, now):
    """Rows past SUB_TTL_H, logged as unsent; the rest returned. A row taken by a pull whose take has
    not lapsed waits for that pull's settle."""
    keep = []
    for r in rows:
        held = r.get("state") == "taken" and now - (r.get("taken_at") or 0) < mail_take_s()
        if now - (r.get("at") or 0) > SUB_TTL_H * 3600 and not held:
            log({"road": "mailbox", "verdict": "unreachable", "target": r.get("target"), "host": r.get("host"),
                 "kind": r.get("kind"), "frame": r.get("frame"), "mail": r.get("id"),
                 "why": "expired after %d h unsent" % SUB_TTL_H, "at": int(now)})
        else:
            keep.append(r)
    return keep


def mail_take(host, dry=False):
    """HOST's rows, marked taken here before HOST posts any (two pulls never take one row at once):
    each waiting row, and each taken one whose take is older than mail_take_s() (a pull that died).
    A take stamps HOST as seen pulling; a dry one writes nothing."""
    now, out = time.time(), []
    with SubsLock(mail_path()):
        if not dry:
            pulls = read_json(mail_path("hail-mailbox-pulls.json"), {})
            if now - (pulls.get(host) or 0) > 3600:   # hourly is fine-grained enough against MAIL_SEEN_H
                pulls[host] = int(now)
                write_json(mail_path("hail-mailbox-pulls.json"), pulls)
        rows = read_subs(mail_path())
        live = expire(rows, now) if not dry else rows
        for r in live:
            if r.get("host") != host:
                continue
            if r.get("state") == "taken" and now - (r.get("taken_at") or 0) < mail_take_s():
                continue
            if not dry:
                r.update(state="taken", taken_at=int(now), token=uuid.uuid4().hex[:12])
            out.append({k: r.get(k) for k in ("id", "token", "target", "kind", "frame", "from", "at", "roads")})
        if not dry and (out or len(live) != len(rows)):
            write_subs(live, mail_path())
    return out


def mail_settle(host, results):
    """What HOST did with the rows it took: a final verdict leaves the box, logged here (road mailbox;
    `ended` is how this Mac learns the session exited); `kept` puts the row back for the next pull.
    A result whose token is not the row's current take is a stale pull's: ignored, counted."""
    now, settled, kept, stale = int(time.time()), 0, 0, 0
    by_id = {r.get("id"): r for r in results if isinstance(r, dict)}
    with SubsLock(mail_path()):
        rows, keep = read_subs(mail_path()), []
        for r in rows:
            res = by_id.pop(r.get("id"), None)
            if res is None or r.get("host") != host or r.get("state") != "taken" or res.get("token") != r.get("token"):
                if res is not None:
                    stale += 1
                keep.append(r)
                continue
            if res.get("verdict") in FINAL_MAIL:
                settled += 1
                log({"road": "mailbox", "verdict": res["verdict"], "target": r.get("target"), "host": host,
                     "kind": r.get("kind"), "frame": r.get("frame"), "mail": r.get("id"), "why": res.get("why"), "at": now})
                continue
            kept += 1
            r["state"], r["last"] = "waiting", res.get("why")
            r.pop("token", None)
            r.pop("taken_at", None)
            keep.append(r)
        stale += len(by_id)
        write_subs(keep, mail_path())
    return {"settled": settled, "kept": kept, "stale": stale}


def registries():
    """Every session registry of this login, each once: the core's session_dirs() (each login dir's
    sessions/, CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR's, every Orca profile's own), else the home folder's .claude/sessions (or
    ASK_SESSIONS_DIR) and the Orca profiles' — a registry is not one folder, so "no record" in one is
    not "ended" (AGENTS.md's trap; helm's PEER_PROBE reads the same)."""
    home = os.path.expanduser("~")
    dirs = [sessions_dir()]
    try:
        import common
        dirs += [str(d) for d in common.session_dirs()]
    except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001 — no core: the folders it would name, read here
        dirs += glob.glob(os.path.join(home, "Library", "Application Support", "orca", "claude-profiles", "*", "home", "sessions"))
    # and every login dir by its name, listed in an accounts file or not: the transcript glob that proves a
    # session ran here reads them all, so the registries that prove it lives must too
    dirs += sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(home, ".claude*", "sessions")))
    out, seen = [], set()
    for d in dirs:
        r = os.path.realpath(d)
        if r not in seen:
            seen.add(r)
            out.append(d)
    return out


TORN_S = 120   # a record file that does not parse is doubt for this long (a write in flight); older is debris


def registry_doubt(sid):
    """(verdict, why) when SID may still live though the adapter listed no live record of it, or None:
    `unreachable` for a live record in a registry the adapter does not post from (an Orca profile's,
    another login's: the socket road cannot reach it, and waiting would not change that); `kept` for a
    record file that does not read. In detail: a record of SID
    in any registry here (the shared one too) whose process lives, judged as the adapter judges it (its
    pid and recorded start, so a reused pid is no proof), or a record file written in the last TORN_S
    that does not parse (one caught mid-rewrite may be SID's; an old one is a crash's debris). `ended` is
    final and stops a sender's updates, so any doubt keeps the row for the next bell (AGENTS.md: "no
    record" is unknown, never ended)."""
    ctx = harness().Ctx()
    mod = ctx.adapter("claude-code")
    same = getattr(mod, "_same_process", None)
    own = os.path.realpath(sessions_dir())   # the registry the socket road posts from
    for reg in registries():
        for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(reg, "*.json")):
            try:
                with open(p) as f:
                    d = json.load(f)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                try:
                    if time.time() - os.path.getmtime(p) < TORN_S:
                        return "kept", "%s does not read (a record mid-rewrite may be %s's)" % (p, sid)
                except OSError:
                    pass
                continue
            if not isinstance(d, dict) or d.get("sessionId") != sid:
                continue
            pid = d.get("pid")
            if not isinstance(pid, int) or pid <= 0:
                continue
            try:
                alive = same(ctx, pid, d.get("procStart")) if same and d.get("procStart") else (mod._alive(pid) if hasattr(mod, "_alive") else True)
            except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001 — not known dead
                alive = True
            if alive and os.path.realpath(reg) == own:   # live where the adapter reads, missed this pass (a record mid-rewrite)
                return "kept", "%s lives in %s but was not listed this pass" % (sid, reg)
            if alive:
                return "unreachable", "%s lives in %s, a registry the socket road does not post from" % (sid, reg)
    return None


def poll_left():
    """Seconds left before the bell kills this pull (ASK_POLL_DEADLINE, which `ask poll` gives each job),
    or None outside the bell."""
    try:
        return float(os.environ["ASK_POLL_DEADLINE"]) - time.time()
    except (KeyError, ValueError):
        return None


def readback_s():
    return env_float("HAIL_READBACK_S", 10)   # the Claude Code adapter's read-back, which a post waits out


def mail_deliver(row, dry=False, allowed=None, before_post=None):
    """One taken row, posted here: {verdict, why}, verdict one of FINAL_MAIL, `kept` (busy, a post
    that did not go through, a session not known here: the next pull tries again) or dry-run.
    ALLOWED: this Mac's hail.roads, read once per pull; the row's own `roads` (the sender's) narrow it
    further. BEFORE_POST runs right before the socket post (the ledger's provisional mark)."""
    f, ref = row.get("frame") or "", row.get("target") or ""
    # the frame came from another Mac's file: the peer half's checks, never trusted as written
    bad = ("the row has no frame" if not f else
           "the frame is not a HAIL frame" if not FRAME_RE.match(f) else
           "the frame is more than one line" if CTRL_RE.search(f) else
           "the frame is %d characters, over %d" % (len(f), FRAME_MAX) if len(f) > FRAME_MAX else
           "the frame carries an answer (K13)" if ANSWER_RE.search(f) else
           "the row names no session" if not ref else None)
    if bad:
        return {"verdict": "refused", "why": bad}
    H = harness()
    rec, why = target_of({"ref": ref})
    if why:
        return {"verdict": "refused", "why": why}
    if rec is not None and rec.get("state") not in H.FINAL:
        if rec.get("harness") != "claude-code":
            return {"verdict": "unreachable", "why": "%s is a %s session: the mailbox posts to Claude Code sessions only" % (ref, rec.get("harness"))}
        if rec.get("session_id") and rec.get("session_id") == os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID"):
            # a pull run by hand in the target session: the row is another Mac's, the bell posts it
            return {"verdict": "kept", "why": "the pull runs in the target session: the bell posts it"}
        allowed = roads() if allowed is None else allowed
        if "socket" not in allowed and ROADS_UNREAD:
            return {"verdict": "kept", "why": "%s does not read: no road until it does" % surfaces_file()}
        if "socket" not in allowed:
            return {"verdict": "unreachable", "why": "the socket road is not in this Mac's hail.roads"}
        # the sender's roads only narrow: a `roads` that is there and no list (a name, an object) is no road, never
        # all; null is a row from before rows carried roads (the take hands an absent key on as null)
        if row.get("roads") is not None and not (isinstance(row["roads"], list) and "socket" in row["roads"]):
            return {"verdict": "unreachable", "why": "the socket road is not in the sender's hail.roads"}
        left = poll_left()
        if not dry and left is not None and left < readback_s() + 30:
            return {"verdict": "kept", "why": "the bell's deadline is %d s out: posted at the next one" % max(left, 0)}
        if before_post and not dry:
            before_post()
        road, res = adapter_road(rec, {"kind": row.get("kind") or "event", "frame": f, "dry": dry, "idle_s": IDLE_S})
        if res["verdict"] == "unreachable" and res.get("raised"):
            # the adapter raised mid-send: the post may have gone out, so never again (at most once)
            return {"verdict": "held", "why": "the post may have gone out: %s" % res["why"]}
        if res["verdict"] in ("refused", "unreachable"):
            # at work, or a post that did not go through (its inbox refused one connect, its record mid-rewrite):
            # the next bell tries again, and a session that has gone by then reads `ended`
            return {"verdict": "kept", "why": res["why"]}
        return {"verdict": res["verdict"], "why": res["why"]}
    sid = (rec or {}).get("session_id") or ref
    doubt = registry_doubt(sid)
    if doubt:
        return {"verdict": doubt[0], "why": doubt[1]}
    if (rec is not None and rec.get("state") in H.FINAL) or (SID_RE.match(sid) and cc_transcript(sid)):
        return {"verdict": "ended", "why": "%s has ended on %s" % (sid, H.machine())}
    return {"verdict": "kept", "why": "no session on %s answers to %r, and none by that id ran here: not known to have ended" % (H.machine(), ref)}


def cc_transcript(sid):
    """SID's transcript under any login's config dir here, or None (the Claude Code adapter's reading)."""
    mod = harness().Ctx().adapter("claude-code")
    try:
        return mod.transcript(sid) if mod is not None and hasattr(mod, "transcript") else None
    except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001 — unknown, never ended
        return None


def mail_bundle(results=None):
    """What a peer's `python3 -` runs for --take and --settle: this file alone (no adapters: those
    halves read and write the mailbox, nothing else). RESULTS, a settle's, ride in front of it on stdin,
    never in argv, where a long take (hundreds of rows) passes the system's argument limit."""
    with open(os.path.abspath(__file__)) as f:
        head = "HAIL_EMBEDDED = {'harness': None, 'adapters': {}}\n"
        if results is not None:
            head += "HAIL_RESULTS = %s\n" % ascii(json.dumps(results, ensure_ascii=True))
        return head + f.read()


def done_key(host, row):
    return "%s:%s" % (host, row.get("id"))


def mail_done(update=None):
    """The receiver's ledger of final verdicts by "<sender>:<row id>", pruned past SUB_TTL_H + a day;
    UPDATE ({key: verdict record, or None to drop it}) is written under its lock. Returns the ledger."""
    path, now = mail_path("hail-mailbox-done.json"), time.time()
    with SubsLock(path):
        led = read_json(path, {})
        if update:
            led.update(update)
            led = {k: v for k, v in led.items() if isinstance(v, dict) and now - (v.get("at") or 0) < (SUB_TTL_H + 24) * 3600}
            write_json(path, led)
    return led


def mail_peer_state(host, ok):
    """True when HOST's answer changed since the last pull (a line is due): one line when a peer goes
    quiet and one when it answers again, never one every bell for a Mac that sleeps."""
    path = mail_path("hail-mailbox-peers.json")
    with SubsLock(path):
        st = read_json(path, {})
        was = st.get(host)
        if was == ok:
            return False
        st[host] = ok
        write_json(path, st)
    return not (was is None and ok)


def mail_pull(dry=False):
    """This Mac's rows from each peer it has an ssh alias for, posted here and settled there: (results, rc).
    rc 3 when a settle failed (the rows wait out their take, then settle from the ledger)."""
    H = harness()
    me, out, rc, allowed = H.machine(), [], 0, roads()
    if not dry:   # this Mac's own box ages here too: rows for a host that stopped pulling still expire
        with SubsLock(mail_path()):
            rows = read_subs(mail_path())
            live = expire(rows, time.time())
            if len(live) != len(rows):
                write_subs(live, mail_path())
    for host, alias in sorted(H.peers().items()):
        rows, why, _ = on_peer(host, alias, ["mail", "--take", me] + (["--dry-run"] if dry else []), src=mail_bundle(), want=list,
                               quiet=True, timeout=30)
        if why:
            if not dry and mail_peer_state(host, False):
                out.append({"from": host, "verdict": "unreachable", "why": why + " (said once, until it answers again)"})
            continue
        if not dry and mail_peer_state(host, True):
            out.append({"from": host, "verdict": "answered", "why": "%s answers again" % host})
        led = mail_done() if rows and not dry else {}
        results = []
        for row in rows:
            done = led.get(done_key(host, row))
            left = poll_left()
            if not dry and not done and left is not None and left < readback_s() + 60:
                # room for a post's read-back and the settle's ssh: the rest wait for the next bell, settled now
                res = {"verdict": "kept", "why": "the bell's deadline is %d s out: posted at the next one" % max(left, 0)}
            elif done:   # posted by an earlier pull whose settle was lost: settled again, never posted twice
                res = {"verdict": done.get("verdict"), "why": done.get("why"), "again": True}
            else:
                key, marked = done_key(host, row), []
                mark = lambda key=key, marked=marked: (marked.append(True), mail_done({key: {
                    "verdict": "held", "why": "posted; the pull ended before its read-back", "at": int(time.time()), "provisional": True}}))
                try:
                    res = mail_deliver(row, dry, allowed, before_post=mark)
                except Exception as e:   # noqa: BLE001 — one bad row never costs the pull: the next one tries it
                    res = {"verdict": "kept", "why": "the post failed: %s" % e}
                at = int(time.time())
                try:   # a ledger that cannot be written costs that write, never the pull (its rows settle all the same)
                    if not dry and res["verdict"] not in FINAL_MAIL and marked:
                        mail_done({key: None})   # kept: no post went out (a refused or failed one), the next bell may post it
                    if not dry and res["verdict"] in FINAL_MAIL:
                        mail_done({key: {"verdict": res["verdict"], "why": res.get("why"), "at": at}})
                except OSError as e:
                    warn("the mailbox ledger could not be written (%s)" % e)
                if not dry and res["verdict"] in FINAL_MAIL:
                    log({"road": "mailbox", "verdict": res["verdict"], "target": row.get("target"), "host": me, "from": host,
                         "kind": row.get("kind"), "frame": row.get("frame"), "mail": row.get("id"), "why": res.get("why"), "at": at})
            res.update(mail=row.get("id"), token=row.get("token"), target=row.get("target"), kind=row.get("kind"), host=me)
            results.append(res)
        if results and not dry:
            back = [{"id": r["mail"], "token": r["token"], "verdict": r["verdict"], "why": r.get("why")} for r in results]
            got, why, _ = on_peer(host, alias, ["mail", "--settle", me], src=mail_bundle(back), timeout=30)
            if why:   # unsettled: the take lapses after mail_take_s(), and the next take settles from the ledger
                out.append({"from": host, "verdict": "unreachable", "why": "settle: " + why})
                rc = 3
        for r in results:
            r.pop("token", None)
            r["from"] = host
            out.append(r)
    return out, rc


def cmd_mail(args):
    if args.get("take") or args.get("settle"):
        host = (args.get("take") or args.get("settle") or "").lower()
        if not HOST_RE.match(host):
            sys.exit("hail: %r is no host name" % host)
        if args.get("take"):
            print(json.dumps(mail_take(host, bool(args.get("dry-run"))), ensure_ascii=False))
            return 0
        try:
            results = json.loads(args.get("results") or globals().get("HAIL_RESULTS") or "")
        except ValueError:
            sys.exit("hail: --settle needs --results, a JSON list")
        if not isinstance(results, list):
            sys.exit("hail: --settle needs --results, a JSON list")
        print(json.dumps(mail_settle(host, results), ensure_ascii=False))
        return 0
    if args.get("pull"):
        out, rc = mail_pull(bool(args.get("dry-run")))
        if args.get("json"):
            print(json.dumps(out, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))
        else:
            for r in out:
                if r.get("mail"):
                    print("%s  %s %s by mail from %s%s" % (r["mail"], r.get("target"), r["verdict"], r["from"],
                                                          " (kept)" if r["verdict"] == "kept" else ""))
                else:
                    print("hail mail: %s: %s" % (r["from"], r.get("why")))
        return rc
    rows = read_subs(mail_path())
    if args.get("json"):
        print(json.dumps(rows, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))
    elif not rows:
        print("no mailbox rows")
    else:
        for r in rows:
            print("%s  %s  %-10s %s  %s  %s%s" % (r.get("id"), time.strftime("%m-%d %H:%M", time.localtime(r.get("at") or 0)),
                                                 r.get("host"), r.get("target"), r.get("kind"), r.get("state"),
                                                 ": " + r["last"] if r.get("last") else ""))
    return 0


# ---- the command line ----------------------------------------------------------------------

VALUED = ("--text", "--file", "--kind", "--about", "--thread", "--host", "--when", "--frame", "--roads",
          "--take", "--settle", "--results")
FLAGS = ("--dry-run", "--json", "--fulfil", "--peer-half", "--no-file", "--sender-fenced", "--pull")


def parse(argv):
    a = {}
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        x = argv[i]
        if x in ("-h", "--help"):
            print(__doc__)
            sys.exit(0)
        if x in FLAGS:
            a[x[2:]] = True
        elif x in VALUED and i + 1 < len(argv):
            a[x[2:]] = argv[i + 1]
            i += 1
        elif not x.startswith("-") and "ref" not in a:
            a["ref"] = x
        else:
            sys.exit("hail: unexpected %r\n%s" % (x, USAGE))
        i += 1
    return a


def emit(rec, as_json):
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(rec, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))
        return
    print("%s via %s → %s%s" % (rec["verdict"], rec.get("road") or "-", rec.get("target"),
                                ": " + rec["why"] if rec.get("why") else ""))
    for road, why in rec.get("tried") or []:
        print("  tried %s: %s" % (road, why))


def main(argv):
    if argv[:1] == ["subs"]:
        return cmd_subs(parse(argv[1:]))
    if argv[:1] == ["mail"]:
        return cmd_mail(parse(argv[1:]))
    a = parse(argv)
    if a.get("peer-half"):   # a peer's half of --host: the adapter roads, the frame as sent
        print(PEER_MARK, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        # a public flag on the same binary: the frame it posts must still be one hail's frame
        f = a.get("frame") or ""
        bad = ("--peer-half needs --frame" if not f else
               "the frame is not a HAIL frame" if not FRAME_RE.match(f) else
               "the frame is more than one line" if CTRL_RE.search(f) else
               "the frame is %d characters, over %d" % (len(f), FRAME_MAX) if len(f) > FRAME_MAX else
               "the frame carries an answer (K13)" if ANSWER_RE.search(f) else None)
        if bad:
            print(json.dumps({"road": None, "verdict": "refused", "target": a.get("thread") or a.get("ref"),
                              "why": bad, "tried": []}, ensure_ascii=False))
            return 2
        own = roads()
        msg = {"kind": a.get("kind") or "event", "frame": f, "dry": bool(a.get("dry-run")), "idle_s": IDLE_S,
               "sender_fenced": bool(a.get("sender-fenced")),
               # the sender's hail.roads: the peer takes only what the sender's row allows
               # and this Mac's own row, as the mailbox's receiver honours both
               "roads": [r for r in (",".join(ROADS) if a.get("roads") is None else a["roads"]).split(",") if r in ROADS and r in own]}
        rec = deliver(dict(a, host="here"), msg)
        print(json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False))
        return 0
    if not a.get("ref"):
        sys.exit(USAGE)
    if bool(a.get("text")) == bool(a.get("file")):
        sys.exit("hail: one of --text or --file\n" + USAGE)
    if a.get("file"):
        try:
            with open(a["file"]) as f:
                a["text"] = f.read()
        except OSError as e:
            sys.exit("hail: --file: %s" % e)
    kind = a.get("kind") or "event"
    if kind not in KINDS:
        sys.exit("hail: --kind is one of %s" % ", ".join(KINDS))
    when = a.get("when") or "now"
    if when not in ("now", "idle"):
        sys.exit("hail: --when is now or idle")
    dry = bool(a.get("dry-run"))
    about = parse_about(a["about"]) if a.get("about") else None
    if about:
        about["sha"] = sha_of(about)
    rec = {"road": None, "verdict": None, "target": a.get("thread") or a["ref"], "kind": kind, "tried": []}
    why = text_refusal(a["text"])
    if why:
        rec.update(verdict="refused", why=why)
    else:
        msg = {"kind": kind, "frame": frame(kind, a["text"], about, sender()), "dry": dry, "idle_s": IDLE_S, "roads": roads(),
               "space": os.environ.get("HAIL_SPACE") or None, "no_file": bool(a.get("no-file")), "sender_cwd": os.getcwd(),
               # what a non-Claude road's vendor fence judges on the sender's side: its cwd and the --about repo
               "fence_paths": [os.getcwd()] + [p for p in ([repo_dir(about["repo"])] if about else []) if p]}
        if CTRL_RE.search(msg["frame"]):   # a control character in the text, or a line break in the sender's name
            rec.update(verdict="refused", why="the frame is more than one line: a hail is one line, which every receiver refuses otherwise")
        # the receiver's other frame checks (mail_deliver, the peer half), judged here first: a mailbox row
        # would otherwise say `queued` and be refused for good a bell later, seen only in hail.jsonl
        elif len(msg["frame"]) > FRAME_MAX:
            rec.update(verdict="refused", why="the frame is %d characters, over %d: a shorter sender name (HAIL_FROM) or --about, which every receiver refuses otherwise" % (len(msg["frame"]), FRAME_MAX))
        elif ANSWER_RE.search(msg["frame"]):
            rec.update(verdict="refused", why="the frame carries an answer (K13), in the sender's name: every receiver refuses it")
        else:
            rec = deliver(a, msg)
        # --when idle: a target still at work is a subscription, not a refusal
        if when == "idle" and rec["verdict"] == "refused" and (rec.get("road") in ("socket", "orca") or rec.get("busy")):
            rec = subscribe(a, msg, rec)
    if about and not about.get("sha") and rec.get("verdict") != "refused":
        rec.setdefault("notes", []).append("no commit found for %s:%s: the frame has no @sha" % (about["repo"], about["branch"]))
    rec["at"] = int(time.time())
    if dry:
        rec["dry_run"] = True
    else:
        log(rec)
    emit(rec, a.get("json"))
    return EXIT.get(rec["verdict"], 3)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
